# Line endings.
#
# Edited on Windows, run on Linux: without this the two disagree about every file —
# `core.autocrlf` alone leaves CRLF in one working tree and LF in the other, invisible until
# something diffs, or until a shell script picks up a `\r` and fails with an error that names
# the wrong thing entirely.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than plain `text=auto`: the repository stores LF either way, but this also
# checks out LF on Windows, so both machines see identical bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
